    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_cf537049",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "meme_concept",
      "label": "Meme Concept: 'The Only Fuck I Have Left to Give'",
      "description": "This meme format is widely used on social media to humorously or ironically express giving one's last effort, energy, or resources, often in a context of exhaustion, resignation, or dramatic finality. The phrase 'the only fuck I have left to give' is a colloquial, vulgar expression implying that the speaker has nothing more to offer — physically, emotionally, or otherwise — and is using the act of throwing something (often symbolically) to represent this final act. The phrase 'andddddd there it goes' reinforces the dramatic, almost theatrical, nature of the gesture, implying the culmination of effort or the release of all remaining resources. This concept relies on cultural understanding of military imagery, exhaustion tropes, and internet humor involving self-deprecating or exaggerated gestures.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_aa3a523e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_265c7f8c",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "military_context",
      "label": "Military Context and Stereotypes",
      "description": "The image of a soldier in uniform, often associated with discipline, sacrifice, and combat, is used here to evoke the stereotype of the 'soldier as a giver of all' — a trope that implies the soldier has given everything for duty, honor, or mission. This stereotype is often used in media and memes to symbolize ultimate sacrifice or extreme effort. The soldier's gesture of throwing something (possibly a grenade or a symbolic object) is interpreted as a metaphor for giving one's last resource — a concept that is culturally understood through military narratives and popular media depictions of soldiers. The meme leverages this visual and cultural association to create a humorous or dramatic effect.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_aa3a523e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8b0685d1",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "vulgar_language_use",
      "label": "Use of Vulgar Language in Memes",
      "description": "The phrase 'the only fuck i have left to give' relies on the use of the word 'fuck,' which is a profanity commonly used in informal, colloquial, or humorous contexts. The use of such language in memes is a cultural phenomenon that often serves to convey intensity, authenticity, or irreverence. While the word 'fuck' is not visible in the image, its inclusion in the text overlay is essential to understanding the tone and intent of the meme. The meme's humor or impact is partly derived from the shock value or the casualness of using such language in a context that might otherwise be serious or dramatic.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_aa3a523e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_dfd69c4e",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "dramatic_gesture_stereotype",
      "label": "Dramatic Gesture Stereotype",
      "description": "The soldier's raised arm and throwing motion is a visual trope often used in media and memes to convey a sense of finality, release, or dramatic action. This gesture is culturally associated with 'throwing something away' — whether literally (like a grenade) or metaphorically (like giving up). The meme relies on viewers understanding this gesture as a symbolic act of surrender or exhaustion, which is a common trope in both military and civilian contexts. The exaggerated 'andddddd there it goes' text reinforces this dramatic interpretation, which is a common feature of internet humor and meme culture.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_aa3a523e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_258da9f0",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "resignation",
      "label": "resigned emotion",
      "description": "The emotion of giving up or having nothing left to offer, conveyed through the soldier's gesture and the text overlay. The phrase 'the only fuck i have left to give' expresses a sense of exhaustion and finality, while 'andddddd there it goes' dramatizes the act of releasing one's last resources.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_aa3a523e"
